    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0317" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9839</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-04T16:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 5, 2.57 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1248 [<hi rendition="#italic">1579</hi>]. Your 1248, May 3, 4 p.m. Took up matter
                    immediately and confidentially with Baron
                        Sonnino who thinks that such a declaration will serve most useful
                    purpose and have an important effect. It will shake up Turkey and Bulgaria, and
                    will prove a <pb facs="0318" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/> material aid against
                    Austria and also Germany. He expressed himself as very confident of the material
                    aid which the declaration would render to the Allied cause.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
